**Final submission: T4C — deviation, preferred-level redline at §14.2.2 (validated ok:true, minimality ok).**

Repair made this pass: Operation 2 was deleted. The insertion "or has obtained Regulatory Approval prior to such termination" was Customer-adverse (it extended PB's ARTICLE 6 payment obligation into a scenario the original clause never reached) and was not required by any selected element — the retained sentence is merely silent about a post-Approval exit, not contradictory. That silence is now flagged in the comment instead.

The proposal is a single surgical replace carrying all four preferred elements:
1. Unconditional PB convenience right — the $60M spend gate and the pre-first-Approval cut-off are removed;
2. Thirty (30) days' prior written notice — the blank [***] is resolved;
3. SFJ refunds pro rata any amounts prepaid by PB (broadened from "fees" because this Agreement has no defined fee concept; harmless if nothing is prepaid);
4. Express bar on SFJ convenience termination during the Term.

Everything else in §14.2.2 survives verbatim: the 300% Development Cost consideration for the Trial Data Package, the ARTICLE 6 Approval Payment carry-over, the Section 6.7 Buy-Out offset, the Section 6.2 adjustment and the credit for amounts previously paid.

Client-facing caveat now in the comment: this exit is unconditional but not free — 300% of Development Costs plus continuing Approval Payments — so "convenience" here is not "without penalty" in the playbook's summary sense; repricing that buy-out is a separate commercial ask, as is §14.2.10's near-discretionary JSC-disagreement right if SFJ resists the new no-convenience sentence.
